    "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\n`:amd: (MI300) MoE Kernels Shard 1` keeps hitting its 55-minute timeout even though all of its tests pass (for example amd-ci #14545, and ci #95182 on #59677).\r\n\r\nThe cause is the AITER `test_modular_kernel_combinations.py` command:\r\n- Its FP8 per-tensor and per-token cases compile CK 2-stage MoE kernels while the test runs, about 10.5 minutes per kernel. The prebuilt kernels in the image can't be used for these cases on gfx942 until https://github.com/ROCm/aiter/issues/5766 is fixed.\r\n- The command is split across 5 shards by hashing test names. Tests that need the same kernel land on different shards, so the same 4 kernels get compiled 12 times per run.\r\n- Shard 1 needed all 4 kernels, so it took about 55 minutes while shards 2-5 took 28-38 minutes.\r\n\r\nThis PR moves that command out of the 5 shards into two separate jobs:\r\n- `:amd: (MI300) MoE Kernels AITER FP8 Per-Tensor`: `-k \"not multigpu and (fp8_tensor or AiterFp8TensorExperts)\"`\r\n- `:amd: (MI300) MoE Kernels AITER Other`: `-k \"not multigpu and not (fp8_tensor or AiterFp8TensorExperts)\"`, the exact opposite filter, so no test is left out.\r\n\r\nEach new job keeps the original job's trigger paths, hardware and pool. The 5 MoE Kernels shards keep the other two commands.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n- Took the per-test logs from ci #95182 and mapped each of the 54 single-GPU AITER test cases to the kernels it compiles.\r\n- Checked the two `-k` filters against those test names: together they select the same 54 tests, with no overlap.\r\n- Rendered `test-amd.yaml` with the amd-ci template (`test-template-amd.j2`, minijinja-cli 2.3.1) for a PR run and a nightly run. Both new jobs appear on `mi300_1` with the filters intact.\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\nExpected time, based on the ci #95182 timings:\r\n\r\n| Job | Before | After |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| MoE Kernels Shard 1 | ~55 min (timeout) | ~10-15 min |\r\n| MoE Kernels Shards 2-5 | 28-38 min | ~10-15 min |\r\n| AITER FP8 Per-Tensor (new) | - | ~39 min (16 tests, 3 kernel compiles) |\r\n| AITER Other (new) | - | ~38 min (38 tests, 2 kernel compiles) |\r\n\r\nThe longest MoE job goes from about 55 minutes to about 40, and total machine time drops by about 50 minutes per run. I'll confirm with `/amd-ci run` on this PR.",
